      "13-gauge stamped deck is the thinnest on this list",
      "Hydro-Gear EZT 2200 transmissions are listed as non-serviceable"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A good flat-acre mower at the lowest price here, held back mainly by its stamped deck and sealed transmissions.",
    "description": "The Ultima ZT1 42 is the mower to buy if you want a zero turn for a flat acre or so and do not want to spend more than necessary. Cub Cadet lists an MSRP from $3,429 for this configuration, model 17AIEACSA10, with a 726cc Kawasaki FR651V twin rated at 21.5 hp. It has the widest cut height range here, 1 to 4.5 inches across 15 positions, and a 7 mph forward speed, slightly quicker than the Husqvarnas. The trade-offs are honest ones for the price. The deck is stamped from 13-gauge steel, thinner than the 10-gauge fabricated decks on the Toro and Husqvarnas, and stamped decks are more prone to bending if you hit roots and stones. The drive is a pair of Hydro-Gear EZT 2200 transmissions, which Cub Cadet lists as maintenance-free and not serviceable, so they are replaced rather than rebuilt when they eventually wear. Cub Cadet does back the machine well: a 3-year unlimited-hour residential warranty plus lifetime limited coverage on both the frame and the deck shell. The 20 inch high-back seat has an adjustment knob but no armrests. On a flat, open acre with weekly mowing, it does the job well."
  },
  {
    "id": "john-deere-z330m",
    "name": "John Deere Z330M ZTrak 48 in. Zero Turn",
    "category": "Residential, 48\" 10-Gauge Accel Deep Deck",
    "badge": "Best Dealer-Backed",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "48 inch Accel Deep deck in 10-gauge steel",
      "23 hp Kawasaki FR691V V-twin",
      "20 inch high-back seat with spring suspension",
      "Deere dealer network for parts and service",
      "Material collection and mulch kits designed for the deck"
