      "Deere's February 2026 list price is $3,899 for the base 48 inch machine, more than the Husqvarna Z242F",
      "Hydro-Gear EZT transmissions, an entry-level residential unit"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A well-made 48 inch residential mower for buyers who want a local dealer behind it.",
    "description": "The Z330M is the heart of John Deere's Z300 residential line and the model most homeowners will be quoted at a Deere dealer. Deere's February 2026 price list gives a suggested list price of $3,899 for the base machine with the 48 inch Accel Deep deck, which Deere describes as forged from 10-gauge steel, with 1.25 to 4.5 inch cutting heights, a wash port and a three-point mounting system. A 54 inch deck is available. Power is a 23 hp Kawasaki FR691V V-twin with full-pressure lubrication and an oil filter. Drive is a pair of Hydro-Gear EZT transmissions at 7.0 mph forward and 3.5 mph reverse, the entry residential drive, which is the main thing holding it back from a higher rating here. The seat is a 20 inch high back with spring suspension, and Deere fits 11-position adjustable levers with three height settings, which helps operators of different heights. Listed weight is 598 pounds, with a 3 gallon fuel tank and 20 by 10 rear tires. The real reason to choose it is the dealer: Deere's network is the deepest in rural America, and service, parts and the Deere material collection system are easy to get. On one to two and a half acres, it is a sound buy."
  },
  {
    "id": "ariens-zenith-60",
    "name": "Ariens Zenith 60 in. Zero Turn Mower 991158",
    "category": "Prosumer-Residential, 60\" 10-Gauge 5.5\" Deep Deck",
    "badge": "Best for 4 Acres & Rough Ground",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "60 inch ENVY Elite deck, 5.5 inches deep, from 10-gauge steel",
      "Serviceable Hydro-Gear ZT-3100 transaxles per retailer spec listings",
      "23.5 hp, 726cc Kawasaki FX730V, a commercial-series engine",
      "Integrated seat isolation dampers",
      "4-year / 750-hour warranty as listed by Ariens"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "60 inch width needs wide gates and a big shed",
      "Costs far more than the 42 and 48 inch picks, and overkill under three acres"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The step-up for four acres or rough ground: serviceable transaxles and a deep 60 inch deck, short of a full commercial price.",
    "description": "The Zenith sits at the top of what a homeowner should call residential, and it is the pick for properties at the four-acre end of this guide or with rough ground that punishes lighter machines. Ariens fits a 60 inch ENVY Elite deck that is 5.5 inches deep and built from 10-gauge steel; the extra depth helps it lift and discharge thick or wet grass that a shallow 42 inch deck would leave in clumps. The engine is a 23.5 hp, 726cc Kawasaki FX730V, from Kawasaki's commercial FX line rather than the residential FR engines on most of this list. Retailer spec listings for model 991158 name Hydro-Gear ZT-3100 transaxles, which are serviceable, with changeable fluid, rather than the sealed EZT units on the cheaper mowers; confirm it at the dealer, because Ariens' own page does not name them. Ariens lists integrated seat isolation dampers to cut vibration, and a 4-year or 750-hour warranty. The downsides are the size and the price. A 60 inch deck will not fit through many garden gates, it needs a deep shed bay, and it costs far more than the 42 and 48 inch machines here, money you only recover on large or rough properties. On three to four acres of uneven ground, it is the residential mower that will last longest."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Residential Zero Turn Mower",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-residential-zero-turn-mower/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best residential zero turn mower?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most homeowners on one to two acres, the Toro TimeCutter MyRIDE 42 (75747) is our pick, combining a 10-gauge fabricated deck, Hydro-Gear ZT-2100 transmissions and MyRIDE suspension at a $4,499 MSRP. For two to four acres, the Husqvarna Z254FX's 54 inch fabricated deck and suspension seat are the better fit."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What size zero turn does a homeowner need?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A 42 inch deck suits up to about two acres and fits most garden gates. A 48 inch deck suits two to two and a half acres, a 54 inch deck two to four acres, and a 60 inch deck three to four acres of open or rough ground. Check gate and shed widths before you decide."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a fabricated deck worth it on a residential mower?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Usually, yes. A fabricated 10-gauge deck holds its shape after hitting roots and stones better than a 13-gauge stamped deck. In 2026 the price gap is small: the Husqvarna Z242F Special Edition's fabricated deck costs $70 more at MSRP than the Cub Cadet ZT1 42's stamped deck. On a flat, clear lawn, stamped is still fine."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long do residential zero turn mowers last?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends mostly on hours and terrain. Residential warranties suggest the expected duty: Cub Cadet and Toro list 3-year unlimited-hour residential terms, and Ariens 4 years or 750 hours on the Zenith. Owners commonly report sealed EZT transmissions as the first major wear item on hilly or large lots."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are residential zero turns good on hills?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only on gentle slopes. They steer with their rear wheels, so losing grip means losing steering. Follow the slope limit in the operator's manual, mow up and down rather than across, and avoid wet grass. Stronger transmissions and wider rear tires help, but for steep banks a different mower is safer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you buy a residential zero turn mower on Amazon?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Some, yes. The Husqvarna Z242F Special Edition, Husqvarna Z254FX and Ariens Zenith 60 are sold on Amazon. Toro sells the TimeCutter MyRIDE 42 through dealers, and Cub Cadet and John Deere models go through dealers and stores. Check delivery terms and the nearest service center before ordering online."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between a residential and commercial zero turn?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Residential mowers use sealed or light-duty transmissions, 10 to 13 gauge decks and warranties of a few hundred hours, built for 30 to 120 hours a year. Commercial mowers use serviceable heavy-duty transaxles or pumps and wheel motors, 7-gauge decks and warranties written in 1,000-plus hours, at several times the price."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Lawn & Yard Care",
    tags: [
      "best residential zero turn mower",
      "residential zero turn mower",
      "zero turn mower for homeowners",
      "homeowner zero turn",
      "zero turn mower"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Updated November 2026
          </span>
